@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] share-moment-shooting-star
After something is shared into Inventory, while it saves, the share target MUST play
the shooting star moment over the app that shared: the page blurs under a night
sky, a constellation draws itself, one star breaks off and falls, turning colour
once for a Rare find and twice for a Legendary one, lands in a white-out, and the
find's card spins out of it face up with its rarity, stars and points. The card
then turns over into the tag step (share-tag-step-icon-grid); when that ends it
turns back and flies into the backpack at the top right, whose count goes up, as
the page comes back. A tap anywhere or Back while it plays MUST skip the rest of
it and the tag step: the page comes back at once and the find pops into the
backpack. When nothing could be saved the moment MUST fade without the backpack
and the share sheet says why (share-problems-speak-for-thymind). With the
system's animations turned off the share sheet shows instead. The moment MUST
NOT show levels or XP, and the backpack MUST NOT be called a basket.
The moment MUST be the prototype's own moment 03, with all of its animation,
backgrounds and effects: the app plays the prototype's engine itself
(android/moment-web) in a see-through WebView, fed the find's title, site,
number, picture and rarity, and keeps its own sounds, vibrations, blur and tag
step. A redrawing of it that leaves effects out MUST NOT ship in its place. Where
that page cannot play (no WebView, a page error, or not ready within 2.5
seconds) the app's own drawing of the moment SHOULD play instead, so a share
never waits on it; the fallback and its 2.5 seconds are Claude's choice.
Source: Octavian, 5 November 2026, 23:09: "Let's make the 03 shooting star one into a
real thing in the app and build it out fully", moment 03 of the Inventory share
moment prototype; the tap to skip, the backpack and no levels come from his
feedback on that prototype the same day. Playing the prototype's own engine
follows Octavian, 6 November 2026, 13:01: "you didn't include most of the detailed
animations, nor backgrounds, nor effects...it looks like absolute shit in the
actual app."

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] share-tag-step-icon-grid
The tag step after the shooting star MUST be an icon grid on the back of the
find's card, grown to fill the screen at the card's shape. It shows the spaces
as a row of chips, one chosen at a time, with the space Inventory suggests first
but not chosen: a find MUST NOT go into any space the user did not tap, however
the step closes; a Search tags field that can add a new tag; and a grid of tiles, each a
line icon, the tag's name and a check: Inventory's own tags first, on and marked
with the spark (share-sheet-shows-thymind-tags), then the user's, then recent
tags, off. A tap on a tile puts its tag on or takes it off. It MUST go by itself
as share-sheet-fades-by-itself says, its button showing the time left; a tap
outside the card or Back closes it at once. The spaces and tags chosen MUST reach
the saved cards however it closes. A tile's corner marks (the spark and the
check) MUST sit clear of its edge and of its icon, and its name MUST keep room
inside the tile on both sides, at the phone's own text size; a grid with more
rows than fit fades at the bottom rather than cutting a row off. It MUST turn on
from the edge the card turned to and leave by the other, so the turn carries on
one way round.
Source: Octavian's pick of M9 Icon grid on 5 November 2026, 23:27, for the tag step
that follows the shooting star; the icon for each tag is Claude's choice. The M9
frame chose the suggested space from the start; Octavian turned that off on 6 November
2026, 22:14: "Make it so the share doesn't always put my stuff in "Always
Relevant" space. That's super annoying. It shouldn't auto choose a space."
The spacing follows Octavian, 6 November 2026, 13:03: "There's not enough margin on
the side for the small icon, the tags on the card's back don't have proper
spacing inside"; the 10 dp corner inset and the bottom fade are Claude's choice.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] find-rarity-from-library
A find's rarity MUST come from the user's own library, never from chance or
payment: Legendary when no earlier card in the gallery comes from the same
source, Rare when fewer than 5 do, and Common otherwise. A link's source is its
site, without www., m. or mobile., with twitter.com read as x.com and youtu.be
and music.youtube.com as youtube.com; a file's or note's source is its kind.
Rarity sets the star's colours, the card's stars (1, 3, 5) and its points (10,
40, 80). When the library cannot be counted before the star breaks off, the find
is Common.
Source: Octavian's rules for Inventory, 5 November 2026: rarity comes from the
user's own library and points reward saving. The thresholds, the sources and
the point values are Claude's choice and not yet confirmed.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] share-moment-sounds
The moment's sounds MUST play only while the phone's ringer is on, never when it
is silent or on vibrate, and its vibrations MUST follow the phone's touch
feedback setting. The app's sounds MUST play at the phone's media volume, the
one the volume keys set while the app is open, as a game's do.
Source: the sound and feel of the Inventory share moment prototype Octavian heard on
5 November 2026; following the ringer and the touch feedback setting is Claude's
choice. Media volume: Octavian, 6 November 2026, 22:14: "the volume doesn't get
controlled by normal sound volume for some reason? That sucks."
